  clock: 3  # b214
  nonce: b214  # b214
  message: "Fixed in PR #2097. csharp.py: record_declaration (record, record class, record struct) goes through the class branch as kind record (bases incl. the primary-constructor base, attributes, modifiers; stable_id via scoped_stable_id as Java records); _get_enclosing_class walks _CSHARP_TYPE_DECLS. The misbinding had a second cause shared by plain classes: local_symbols keeps every method under its bare name, last in file wins; the same-file branch now prefers Scope.callee and sends a bare cross-type short-name hit through defer_bare_method_call('suffix'). Live repro, same file on dev and branch (record Point(int X,int Y){ M() calls Helper(); Helper() } + class Other{ Helper() }): dev -> symbols M, Helper (no Point), calls M -> Other.Helper; branch -> record Point, Point.M, Point.Helper, calls Point.M -> Point.Helper. Survey on branch: contains Point -> Point.M and Point.Helper, dead-code-maybe finds nothing. A plain class misbound the same way on dev (Point.M -> Other.Helper). CI round 1 failed coverage (csharp.py using-scope lines covered only by an unselected cross-package test); TestCSharpUsingScopeHints fixed it."  # b214
